## When you change this package

- New use case: add it to `Service` in `{{.Name}}.go`, implement it in `service/`, and add a case to `service/service_test.go`.
- New data access: add the method to the interface in `service/service.go`, then implement it in the adapter.
- Business rule violations: return (or wrap with `%w`) a domain error so the transport maps it to the right status.
- Keep the compile-time checks (`var _ {{.Name}}.Service = (*Service)(nil)`) so drift fails the build.
- Keep every handler thin: decode, call the service, encode or acknowledge. Business rules live in `service/`.
{{- if .HTTP}}
- HTTP timeouts belong on the `http.Server` or `http.TimeoutHandler`; always pass `r.Context()` down.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Queue}}
- Message handlers must be idempotent: brokers deliver at least once, so the same message can arrive twice.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Cron}}
- With several replicas, guard jobs with a distributed lock so each runs once per interval.
{{- end}}
- Before finishing: `gofmt -l .`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./...`.
